<title>USA: Wal-Mart Stores opens 28 new stores.</title>
<headline>Wal-Mart Stores opens 28 new stores.</headline>
<dateline>BENTONVILLE, Ark. 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wal-Mart Stores Inc said it opened 28 new stores nationwide, creating 6,175 jobs.</p>
<p>The company, which reported a 6.8 percent increase in same-store sales in December, said the new stores brings the total number of its workers to 675,000. Wal-Mart said the additional employees give it the largest private workforce in the nation.</p>
<p>The company also said it is looking to fill more than 250 management information systems positions, in addition to 100 hourly and 75 management jobs at its headquarters in Arkansas.</p>
<p>Wal-Mart operates 2,736 stores and Sam's Clubs in all 50 states. Its shares were unchanged Wednesday at 23.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
